  "goodToKnow": "Die Kompanie is a military company, a unit of roughly 100 to 250 soldiers led by a Kompaniechef. For a business company, German uses die Firma, das Unternehmen or die Gesellschaft (as in GmbH). The East India Company is die Ostindien-Kompanie, an old use. Kompanie comes from Latin com- + panis (bread), those who share bread, like Kumpan and Kumpel (mate). Plural: die Kompanien."
